  <page_number>53</page_number>
  <running_head>LIBER PRIMVS.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>In-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>lique supplicio affici.</i> In Capito-</l>
    <l n="2">lino : <i>Nam &amp; in crucem milites</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>tulit, &amp; servilibus suppliciis semper</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>affecit.</i> Ergo Livium sic evol-</l>
    <l n="5">ves: <i>De captivis, ut quisque liber,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>aut servus, sua fortuna a quoque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>sumptum supplicium est.</i> Suae for-</l>
    <l n="8">tunae: nempe Crux servo repo-</l>
    <l n="9">sita, gladius aut securis libero.</l>
    <l n="10">Ipsum hoc ita in Hirtio legas:</l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Prehensi servi tres, &amp; unus e legione</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>vernacula. Servi sunt in crucem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>sublati, militi cervices abscisae.</i> Ser-</l>
    <l n="14">vile igitur hoc supplicium, sed</l>
    <l n="15">non ob levem aut cottidianam</l>
    <l n="16">noxam. Horatius indicat:</l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Si quis eum servum, patinam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>qui tollere jussus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Semesos pisces, tepidumque li-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>gurrierit jus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>In cruce suffigat; Labeone infa-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>nior inter</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Sanos dicatur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" type="foot" para="true">1 In Macrino. 2 Lib. III. 3 De bello</l>
    <l n="25" type="foot">Hispan. 4 Lib. I. Serm. III.</l>
  </main_text>
